{"at":1793546368636,"pos":13,"ticket":1,"by":{"kind":"agent","id":"lane","for":"owner"},"fact":{"type":"commented","body":"# Plan: Add slugify: turn a title into a URL slug\n\nAdd a dependency-free title-to-slug helper, with the supported Unicode folding scope made explicit.\n\nSize: 1 story, 1 task, 2 criteria, 295 words.\n\n## User stories\n\n- **blog-author**: As A blog author, I want A URL slug made from a post title, so that Titles with spaces, punctuation and accented letters need a consistent URL form..\n\n## Task 1: Add title-to-slug conversion\n\nIt ends in a pull request.\n\n- [ ] `c1 v1` When A blog author converts three post titles for publication, “Hello, World!” becomes “hello-world”, “Çay Şeker” becomes “cay-seker”, and “!!!” becomes an empty string.\n  - **The whole job.** _Serves blog-author. Check (test): Compare the three title-to-slug results with the expected strings._  \n    _Fixture: One batch of three titles, converted once each: an English greeting, a Turkish title with accents, and punctuation without usable text._\n- [ ] `c2 v1` When A developer reads the public helper documentation, The documentation explains the chosen folding scope, including what happens to letters without a supported ASCII form.\n  - _Serves blog-author. Check (read): Read the helper’s public documentation and compare its folding examples with the resolved folding decision._\n\n## Open questions\n\n1. `q1` How broadly should non-ASCII letters fold into ASCII?\n   - Options: Use Unicode compatibility decomposition and remove combining marks; remaining non-ASCII characters separate words. / Also support an explicitly agreed transliteration table for letters such as ß, æ and ø.\n   - Lean: Use Unicode compatibility decomposition and remove combining marks. This gives Çay Şeker → cay-seker and ﬂower → flower, but Straße → stra-e.\n   - Why: “When they can” does not define a complete folding policy. The folding property, unsupported-character property and documentation criterion depend on this choice.\n\n## Pointers (they bind nobody)\n\n- `src/slug.ts`: The title-to-slug task owns this new file, its named slugify export and its public documentation.\n- `src/slug.test.ts`: The title-to-slug task owns the adjacent tests for all planned properties.\n- `src/title.ts and src/title.test.ts`: Existing examples establish named exports, direct TypeScript imports and adjacent Vitest tests.\n- `AGENTS.md and README.md`: Repository notes require one file per helper, adjacent tests and no runtime dependencies; fast-check is available.\n- `.fabrika/fabrika.toml, package.json and tsconfig.json`: Existing test and typecheck configuration supports this task without exam changes.\n"}}
